 "about": "A saved measurement's menu — from its ⋯, a right-click or a long press in Saved Measurements — in every edition: its items, words, order and icons. 'groups' are its items between separators, in order; each item names what it does ('action'), its words on each platform ('titles': 'mac' and 'ios' are Swift's, 'python' and 'web' the others' — an item with no title for a platform is not on that platform's menu, and a group left empty is not shown), Swift's SF Symbol ('sfSymbol') and the Material Design icon Python and the web draw ('mdi', as Python names it without 'mdi.'; null for an item they do not have). Export writes the file through a save dialog; Share opens the share sheet, which only Swift has. An item ends in '…' when it needs more from the user before it is done, except on iOS and iPadOS (style guide S9).",
